e religious  exemption the only word to describe that  the only way to describe that is that is  just blatant religious hostility it's  unconstitutional it violates federal law  and again we're thrilled that the court  agreed with us and ruled against the  navy and against the department of  defense and we'll see where it goes from  here but martha we look  people's need to read this decision it  is a powerful decision it's available at  first liberty.org people need to read  for themselves this is a blueprint for  how to fight this vaccine mandate the  proper way especially for those who have  a religious objection just like our  clients do and what was their primary  religious objection if you can sum it up  well i mean 35 different navy seals  you're going to have 35 you know  individualized that's the whole point of  this right every person has an  individual religious belief and has the  right to have that religious belief but  many of them they object to the the fact  that the the vaccine was tested or  developed or produced using aborted  fetal cells others just simply prayed to  god they earnestly prayed to god and  said god what do you want me to do and  god said no all right i do not it would  violate their conscience and their  religious convictions to get this  vaccine and under the law that is  absolutely protected in this country  you know and i've heard the point  brought up about general george  washington at valley forge and how he  wanted all of his troops inoculated  against smallpox he did make an  exception for people who had already had  it which i thought was interesting um  what about that precedent  oh well you just said it yourself that  they'll that president washington  general washington at the time even  understood that there was such thing as  natural immunity our pentagon doesn't  seem to get that they they have made no  allowances for natural immunity they've  made no allowances for people with  sincerely held religious beliefs and  